# Windows concrete unit for the file-share seam. Portable header predefs this
# one (mirrors mixa_audio_win32.h.lm1's relationship to mixa_audio.h.lm1):
# MixaShareRequest itself only ever touches this backend through the opaque
# `impl: @: void` field, so nothing here is part of the portable ABI.
#
# Deliberately no `include: "<windows.h>"` (or any WinRT/COM header) here:
# nothing in this stub needs a real Windows type yet (hwnd is opaque @: void,
# not HWND).
#
# CAUTION for the Windows-adapter stage: adding a native include HERE is
# NOT by itself enough to keep it out of the portable contract. The
# portable header still `predef:`s this one, and predef order pulls this
# file's content (includes and all) into any translation unit that only
# wanted mixa_share.h.lm1 -- the same leak, just relocated. Resolve the
# actual portable->concrete dependency (or isolate native includes behind
# an implementation-only boundary that nothing portable-only predefs)
# BEFORE adding COM/WinRT includes, rather than assuming this file is a
# safe place for them. mixa_audio_win32.h.lm1 and mixa_app_win32.h.lm1
# already have this same structural leak today (both predef'd by their
# portable headers, both including windows.h) -- worth fixing there too,
# not a Share-specific problem to solve alone.

struct: MixaShareWin32Ctx
    @: void hwnd
    int: registered
    int: pending
end: MixaShareWin32Ctx
